exports[`each template's output > pass_through_ending, for clients: the snapshot 1`] = `
{
  "html": "<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="utf-8">
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
<meta name="color-scheme" content="light dark">
<meta name="supported-color-schemes" content="light dark">
<title>Calls stop passing through on 6 December</title>
<style>@media (prefers-color-scheme: dark) {
  body, .hd-wrap { background: #0d1117 !important; color: #e6edf3 !important; }
  .hd-muted { color: #9da7b3 !important; }
  a { color: #8cc4ff !important; }
  a.hd-action { background: #e6edf3 !important; color: #0d1117 !important; }
}</style>
</head>
<body style="margin:0;padding:0;background:#ffffff;color:#1f2328;">
<span style="display:none;max-height:0;overflow:hidden;opacity:0;mso-hide:all;">Undo your call forwarding this week, so callers keep reaching you after 6 December.</span>
<div class="hd-wrap" style="max-width:560px;margin:0 auto;padding:24px 16px;font-family:-apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, 'Segoe UI', Roboto, Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif;font-size:16px;line-height:1.5;color:#1f2328;background:#ffffff;">
<p style="margin:0 0 16px;">Radiance Med Spa&#39;s line was set to forward calls to healdesk. Since your service ended, calls still forwarded to us pass straight through to your direct line, and that stops on Sunday 6 December. After that, a call still forwarded to us won&#39;t reach you.</p>
<p style="margin:0 0 16px;">If you haven&#39;t undone the forwarding yet, do it before Sunday 6 December, so callers keep reaching you directly. Follow these AT&amp;T steps, dialling each code from the clinic&#39;s own line:</p>
<ul style="margin:0 0 16px;padding-left:20px;"><li>Cancel busy forwarding on AT&amp;T Phone: *91#</li><li>Cancel no-answer forwarding on AT&amp;T Phone: *93#</li><li>Cancel Safe Call Forwarding on AT&amp;T Phone: *373#</li><li>On AT&amp;T Phone, those codes don&#39;t bring back AT&amp;T voicemail for missed calls. To send unanswered and busy calls to voicemail again on AT&amp;T Phone for Business, sign in to your AT&amp;T account, open Voicemail Settings and set No Answer and Busy Call Forwarding to Forward to Voice Mail; on AT&amp;T Phone at home, ask AT&amp;T to set them back to voicemail.</li><li>On a traditional AT&amp;T landline, call AT&amp;T on 800.288.2020 to remove busy and no-answer forwarding, or to set it back to your voicemail if that&#39;s where it went before.</li><li>On an AT&amp;T mobile line, turn the forwarding off in the phone&#39;s own call-forwarding settings (AT&amp;T lets forwarding be changed only from the phone itself).</li></ul>
<p style="margin:0 0 16px;">Once it&#39;s undone, calls ring your own line as they did before healdesk, and nothing is forwarded to us.</p>
<hr style="border:none;border-top:1px solid #d0d7de;margin:24px 0 16px;">
<p class="hd-muted" style="margin:0 0 6px;color:#57606a;font-size:13px;">You&#39;re receiving this because this is the address on Radiance Med Spa&#39;s healdesk account.</p>
<p class="hd-muted" style="margin:0 0 6px;color:#57606a;font-size:13px;">Replies reach the healdesk team. Please leave out patient details.</p>
<p class="hd-muted" style="margin:0 0 6px;color:#57606a;font-size:13px;">healdesk is a service of Viixi FZC, a company registered under the Sharjah Publishing City Free Zone, United Arab Emirates.</p>
<p class="hd-muted" style="margin:0 0 6px;color:#57606a;font-size:13px;">US mailing address (correspondence only): 800 N King Street, Suite 304-1426, Wilmington, DE 19801, United States</p>
</div>
</body>
</html>",
  "preheader": "Undo your call forwarding this week, so callers keep reaching you after 6 December.",
  "subject": "Calls stop passing through on 6 December",
  "text": "Radiance Med Spa's line was set to forward calls to healdesk. Since your service ended, calls still forwarded to us pass straight through to your direct line, and that stops on Sunday 6 December. After that, a call still forwarded to us won't reach you.

If you haven't undone the forwarding yet, do it before Sunday 6 December, so callers keep reaching you directly. Follow these AT&T steps, dialling each code from the clinic's own line:

- Cancel busy forwarding on AT&T Phone: *91#
- Cancel no-answer forwarding on AT&T Phone: *93#
- Cancel Safe Call Forwarding on AT&T Phone: *373#
- On AT&T Phone, those codes don't bring back AT&T voicemail for missed calls. To send unanswered and busy calls to voicemail again on AT&T Phone for Business, sign in to your AT&T account, open Voicemail Settings and set No Answer and Busy Call Forwarding to Forward to Voice Mail; on AT&T Phone at home, ask AT&T to set them back to voicemail.
- On a traditional AT&T landline, call AT&T on 800.288.2020 to remove busy and no-answer forwarding, or to set it back to your voicemail if that's where it went before.
- On an AT&T mobile line, turn the forwarding off in the phone's own call-forwarding settings (AT&T lets forwarding be changed only from the phone itself).

Once it's undone, calls ring your own line as they did before healdesk, and nothing is forwarded to us.

—
You're receiving this because this is the address on Radiance Med Spa's healdesk account.
Replies reach the healdesk team. Please leave out patient details.
healdesk is a service of Viixi FZC, a company registered under the Sharjah Publishing City Free Zone, United Arab Emirates.
US mailing address (correspondence only): 800 N King Street, Suite 304-1426, Wilmington, DE 19801, United States
",
}
`;

