- On an AT&T mobile line, AT&T lets forwarding be changed only from the phone itself and gives no code for busy or unanswered calls: in the phone's own call-forwarding settings, if they offer forwarding when busy, unanswered or unreachable (AT&T's device help for your phone shows where; some phones offer only all-call forwarding), forward those calls to: +15125550142
- Your assistant gets a call only if nothing else answers it first. If an answering machine, a voicemail box or a closed-hours greeting on your line picks up before the forwarding does, the call stops there, so switch it off or set it to answer later than the forwarding.
- Then test it: call your main number from a phone that isn't on the clinic's account and let it ring unanswered. Your assistant should answer. Test once while you're closed too.

To undo it at any time:

- Cancel busy forwarding on AT&T Phone: *91#
- Cancel no-answer forwarding on AT&T Phone: *93#
- Cancel Safe Call Forwarding on AT&T Phone: *373#
- On AT&T Phone, those codes don't bring back AT&T voicemail for missed calls. To send unanswered and busy calls to voicemail again on AT&T Phone for Business, sign in to your AT&T account, open Voicemail Settings and set No Answer and Busy Call Forwarding to Forward to Voice Mail; on AT&T Phone at home, ask AT&T to set them back to voicemail.
- On a traditional AT&T landline, call AT&T on 800.288.2020 to remove busy and no-answer forwarding, or to set it back to your voicemail if that's where it went before.
- On an AT&T mobile line, turn the forwarding off in the phone's own call-forwarding settings (AT&T lets forwarding be changed only from the phone itself).

Easier with someone on the line? Book a five-minute call and we'll do it with you.

Book a five-minute call: https://app.healdesk.test/help/call

Questions? Reply to this email and a person at healdesk answers.

—
